## 0. Reproduction at base origin/fix/p2-batch-31 (11746adc)

The finding reproduces at the current base: the deploy path produces an image
SBOM nowhere, attests it nowhere, and the docs still record the gap.

    $ git show HEAD:.github/workflows/deploy-do.yml | grep -c attest-sbom
    0
    $ git show HEAD:.github/workflows/sbom.yml | grep retention
      retention-days: 30
    $ git show HEAD:docs/SBOM_PROCESS.md | grep -E 'not attested|no durable release-bound|only produced by'
    - **Image SBOMs are only produced by `build-push.yml`**, which is
    - The image SBOM is an **artifact only**. It is not attested
    - All SBOM artifacts expire after 30 days; there is no durable release-bound

Conclusion: SUPPLY-P3-001 is still open at base. The fix adds digest-bound image
SBOM generation and an `actions/attest-sbom` attestation to each deploy-path
build job (api/worker/web), so a shipped image stays tied to its SBOM after the
30-day artifact window.

No application code changed, so `corepack pnpm --filter api test` was not run
(n/a per the runner: "plus `... test` if code changed").

